Package: veltos-msi-ec
Architecture: all
Depends: python3,
         pkexec,
         kmod,
         ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: dkms,
          linux-headers-amd64
Description: MSI laptops' keyboard light driver (msi-ec), built with DKMS
 The kernel's own msi-ec (Debian 13) only sets an MSI laptop's battery
 charge limits; the driver's own project also lights the keyboard on the
 MSI laptops it knows (Katana, GF, Modern, Prestige, Stealth and others).
 This package carries that source at a pinned version and a helper that
 builds it with DKMS for the running kernel when VeltOS Keyboard Lighting
 asks for it, loads it in place of the kernel's own and removes it again.
 .
 DKMS and the kernel headers are not installed with this package: Keyboard
 Lighting installs them from Debian on the MSI laptops that need them.
